  "summary": {
    "en": "The Cameroonian government has expanded its BIR rapid-intervention force around Lake Chad, deploying drones and joint border patrols to target Anglophone separatists in the Northwest and Southwest. Government troops killed four suspected separatists after a village attack, while a landmine near the border killed eight soldiers and police were wounded in separate attacks in Fundong. Issa Tchiroma’s party was suspended for three months, and Cameroon received a Metal Shark patrol boat to bolster maritime security. President Paul Biya returned to Cameroon, as noted by Genocide Watch. The UCDP recorded 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
    "nb": "Den kamerunske regjeringen har utvidet sin BIR-hurtigintervensjonsstyrke rundt Tsjad-sjøen, og har satt inn droner og felles grensepatruljer for å treffe anglophones separatister i Nordvest og Sørvest. Regjeringsstyrker drepte fire mistenkte separatister etter et landsbyangrep, mens en landmine nær grensen drepte åtte soldater og politiet ble såret i separate angrep i Fundong. Issa Tchiromas parti ble suspendert i tre måneder, og Kamerun mottok en Metal Shark patruljebåt for å styrke maritim sikkerhet. President Paul Biya returnerte til Kamerun, som notert av Genocide Watch. UCDP registrerte 231 kamprelaterte dødsfall i 2024, ifølge UCDP.",
